Aspect          | Applet (DEPRECATED)              | Application
----------------|----------------------------------|------------------
Entry point     | init() / start()                 | public static void main(String[])
Execution       | Browser / appletviewer           | java command on JVM
Class parent    | extends Applet / JApplet         | No special parent
HTML            | Required (<applet> tag)          | Not required
Security        | Sandbox (restricted access)      | Full system access
File I/O        | Blocked by default               | Allowed
Network         | Only to originating server       | Unrestricted
Graphics        | paint(Graphics g) in Applet      | JFrame + paintComponent()
Parameters      | getParameter() from HTML         | args[] or Scanner
Status          | Deprecated Java 9, Removed Java 17 | Current standard

APPLET LIFECYCLE:
Browser loads -> init() -> start() -> paint()
                                   -> stop() [page hidden]
                                   -> start() [page revisited]
Browser closes -> stop() -> destroy()

SECURITY MODEL (Sandbox):
- Cannot read/write local files.
- Cannot execute programs.
- Cannot communicate with servers other than originating host.
- Cannot access system properties.
- Purpose: prevent malicious applets.

